   "confidence": "low",
   "notes": "9 Bene't St (listed, Q26419226), the frontage between the Cambridge Chop House (painted brick, 1 King's Parade) and The Eagle. Warm buff ashlar on all three floors, plain parapet. I only saw it at very oblique angles (photos taken along the pavement). Three upper window bays per floor; some second-floor windows have small wrought-iron balconettes. Ground floor: a tall white door with a fanlight at the west end, then two tall sash openings. A hanging barber sign ('PH, premium cutting') is on this front, but there is no fascia or shopfront. The x positions are estimates."
